Aaron’s descendants received cities in the heartland of Israel, including areas later associated with Jerusalem and the kingdom of Judah. Their placement among the people ensured that priestly instruction, sacrificial worship, and the teaching of God’s law remained accessible throughout the nation. The Aaronic priesthood pointed beyond itself to Jesus Christ, born from Judah and appointed forever as the true High Priest in the order of Melchizedek.

