Gershon was Levi’s firstborn son, and his clan served the Lord by transporting and caring for the tabernacle curtains, coverings, screens, and cords under the oversight of the priests (Numbers 3:21–26; 4:24–28). Their work upheld the holiness and order of Israel’s worship.

