Aaron’s priestly descendants had already received cities in Judah, Simeon, and Benjamin. The other Kohathite families received ten cities from Ephraim, Dan, and the western half-tribe of Manasseh. Although the Levites possessed no separate tribal territory, the Lord provided permanent homes and pasturelands for them throughout Israel, as commanded in Numbers 35:1–8. Their scattered presence enabled them to serve the sanctuary, instruct Israel in God’s law, and remind every tribe that worship and obedience belonged at the center of national life. The Kohathites bore particular responsibility for the most holy furnishings of the tabernacle after the priests had covered them, a duty requiring reverence and careful obedience.

